WEBVTT

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:15.380
I... I'm confused again.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:18.550
Am I here? Or am I there?

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.820
Over there, I'm everywhere. I know that.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:25.320
I'm connected there, after all.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:26.930
Right?

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:29.900
But where is the real me?

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.130
Oh, right. There is no real me.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:37.940
I only exist inside those people who are aware of my existence.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.030
But this me that's talking right now...

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.030
It's me, isn't it?

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:49.890
This me that's talking... This me... Who is it?

00:00:54.010 --> 00:01:00.340
And you don't seem to understand

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:05.540
A shame you seemed an honest man

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:10.290
And all the fears you hold so dear

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:15.560
Will turn to whisper in your ear

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.960
And you know what they say might hurt you

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:21.430
And you know that it means so much

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:26.190
And you don't even feel a thing

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:31.850
I am falling, I am fading

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:35.970
I have lost it all

00:01:54.720 --> 00:02:03.990
I am falling, I am fading, I am drowning

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:06.630
Help me to breathe

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:11.840
I am hurting, I have lost it all

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:14.380
I am losing

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:18.580
Help me to breathe

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:51.350
Arisu!

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:03.680
A body doesn't mean anything to you, right?

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:13.290
Arisu...

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:33.560
No!

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:48.490
I mess up everything I try to do for you, huh, Arisu?

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:51.140
Honest, I...

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.290
Arisu!

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:04.160
Arisu!

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:13.870
I'm sorry...

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:15.840
I'm sorry...

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:18.960
Arisu, I'm sorry...

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.160
I'm done.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.810
Hey, you didn't clean your plate.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:32.500
She says she's on a diet.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:35.180
Tell the whole world, why don't you?

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:43.760
Oh, I might get a package today. It's C.O.D.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:45.460
If it comes, pay for it, okay?

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.680
Computer parts again?

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:01.690
Hey...

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:03.480
Yes?

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:16.050
No, it's nothing.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:28.120
Arisu!

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:33.000
Arisu! We're going out tonight, right?

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:35.140
Cyberia! Cyberia!

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:37.070
Oh. Sure, why not?

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:38.510
I'd better mail her, then.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:43.570
Arisu? Mail who?

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:58.390
Oh, don't tell me you want her to come along again...

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.030
"Her"?

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:10.370
Chisa?

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:11.900
Yeah. Yomoda Chisa.

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:14.870
Arisu, you talked us into taking her to Cyberia once,

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:19.680
but it's like she just didn't care.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:21.450
Inviting her is pointless.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:22.900
Oh, I get it...

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:23.920
Huh?

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:28.430
It's nothing.

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:29.920
I just thought of something strange.

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:32.360
Something strange?

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:35.370
If you don't remember something, it never happened.

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:36.570
Don't remember?

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:39.930
If you aren't remembered, you never existed.

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:43.500
Who are you talking about?

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.440
Who are you talking about?

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:50.080
Like I said. Nobody.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:52.550
Come on, we'd better hit the books.

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:54.510
Arisu!

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.120
Go!

00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:11.710
Man, I gotta do it again?

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:13.400
Come on, one more time!

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:14.640
Hurry up!

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:16.230
Wait for me!

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:19.470
You're such a sucker!

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:23.580
Mail?

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:24.730
What is it?

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:31.840
Who's that girl?!

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.790
I don't know.

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:36.160
Now what?

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:37.740
Hey, nice machine!

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:42.570
Mine's pretty tricked out, too.

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:45.100
Come on! Hurry!

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:48.430
Come on! Come on!

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:50.500
Mom's waiting!

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:53.370
Okay, okay... Bye.

00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:57.310
Let's go!

00:09:57.310 --> 00:09:59.850
Wait! Shoot for it again!

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:04.420
Hurry up, Taro!

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.650
No fair! Shoot for it again!

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:14.190
I'll quit. I'll quit that dump.

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:16.700
The crap they make me do...

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.460
They all underestimate me...

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:22.640
Oh, well.

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:26.180
I'm gonna quit... I'm gonna quit!

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:52.140
I'm gonna quit!

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:53.730
I'm gonna quit today for sure!

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:20.280
What isn't remembered never happened

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:25.080
Memory is merely a record

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:39.550
You just need to rewrite that record

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:37.710
Is that true?

00:11:43.490 --> 00:11:46.830
Present Day

00:11:46.590 --> 00:11:49.690
Present Time

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:49.920
Why are you crying?

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:54.440
Because you deleted yourself from everyone's memory?

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:01.860
But isn't that what you wanted?

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:05.700
Yes, but...

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:11.030
No one is dying, and no one is being hurt.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:14.460
And no one hates you.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:17.460
Yes, but...

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:24.470
Dead people's information isn't leaking out of the Wired anymore.

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:34.050
So Lain doesn't need to be anywhere anymore.

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:37.520
This is what you wanted, isn't it?

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:41.830
You sound just like him.

00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:43.470
Him?

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:45.880
That man never existed now.

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:49.780
Even if he does, he won't get any ideas into his head about being God.

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:52.980
I'm nowhere now...

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:56.780
If I'm nowhere, who am I?

00:13:56.780 --> 00:13:59.360
Where am I?

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:01.020
You yourself said it.

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:05.560
The Wired isn't an upper layer of the real world.

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:08.320
That's what that man was mistaken about.

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:12.100
A network is a field to pass along information.

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:15.870
Information doesn't stand still there.

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:19.020
Information functions by always being in motion.

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:22.020
Really?

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:29.070
People's memories aren't just personal or one part of the history of humanity.

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:34.540
No, not even the shared unconscious.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:38.460
Do you think that humans could create something that could store

00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:41.390
memory that's that vast?

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:46.030
The Wired was just connected to something else...

00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:49.900
But where was it connected to?

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:58.010
Do people really need to know that?

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:04.310
Look at how far they've come without knowing.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:09.860
The human world creates and prays to its various gods,

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:12.460
and humans convince themselves, "This is how the world is."

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:19.080
I don't like how you're saying this.

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:23.600
Either way, it's Lain that's saying it. Me.

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:25.090
You understand that, right?

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:31.170
Oh, right... Lain was never a person, was she?

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:40.680
Lain is omnipresent, existing everywhere.

00:15:40.680 --> 00:15:43.110
Lain watches quietly.

00:15:43.930 --> 00:15:46.590
Right, Lain is God!

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:48.250
No...

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.220
You're wrong!

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:55.490
It'd be so much easier if you became God.

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:58.750
I think it'd be a lot easier than being a human.

00:16:02.510 --> 00:16:06.560
You wouldn't have to do anything. Just stand there and watch.

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:09.280
No one would look down on Lain.

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:12.150
No one would hate Lain.

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:14.310
That's...

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:26.090
Hey, Lain, let's start everything over again from the beginning!

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:29.200
I mean, you did go and reset everything, after all...

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:31.340
Stop it!

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:03.160
Then what are you, Lain?

00:17:05.840 --> 00:17:06.950
I...

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:08.920
I...

00:17:10.350 --> 00:17:12.880
Where am I?

00:17:13.820 --> 00:17:15.340
Come, Lain.

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:37.600
Dad?

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:55.700
You don't need to wear that anymore, Lain.

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:04.970
Dad, do you know?

00:18:04.970 --> 00:18:06.330
What?

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:10.130
I... Everyone, I...

00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:12.240
You love them?

00:18:15.350 --> 00:18:16.980
Isn't that right?

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:27.080
Lain, I'll make us some nice tea next time.

00:18:28.430 --> 00:18:32.880
Hey, with some madeleines! Definitely. They're great!

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:47.280
So memories aren't only of the past, are they?

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:52.430
They can be of right now, or even of tomorrow.

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:00.720
Unbelievable!

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:02.780
Isn't it? But hang on a second...

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:06.890
I listened to what you had to say.

00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:09.390
Very patiently, I might add.

00:19:10.130 --> 00:19:12.970
I get to pick the curtains for the bedroom, right?

00:19:12.970 --> 00:19:14.330
Yes, ma'am.

00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:19.240
Anything you say.

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:21.290
All right, then. That's a good student.

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:25.640
Something wrong?

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:27.080
No.

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:39.420
Sorry, could you wait here a minute?

00:19:39.420 --> 00:19:40.960
Hey, what're you...

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:03.950
Hello.

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:06.080
Hello.

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:10.080
Have we met before? We have, haven't we?

00:20:14.460 --> 00:20:17.060
Did you go to the school I was a student teacher at?

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:19.870
No, that can't be it...

00:20:19.870 --> 00:20:21.090
Let me think...

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:24.090
Pleased to meet you.

00:20:24.710 --> 00:20:25.700
Huh?

00:20:26.540 --> 00:20:28.940
Pleased to meet you. We haven't met before.

00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:32.740
Oh. Well, I'm pleased to meet you, then.

00:20:32.740 --> 00:20:34.520
I'm Arisu.

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:39.120
Strange name, huh? I'm kind of embarrassed about it.

00:20:40.390 --> 00:20:41.650
What's yours?

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:43.820
Lain.

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:46.720
Lain?

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:49.860
A friend of yours?

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:52.060
No, I thought she was someone else.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:55.730
Well, goodbye, Lain.

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:58.840
Maybe we'll run into each other again someday.

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:03.610
Bye.

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:05.080
Bye, Lain.

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:20.520
You're right. We can see each other anytime.

00:21:40.550 --> 00:21:44.880
I'm here, so I'll be with you forever.

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:19.430
nan no tsumi mo nai hazu na no ni

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:19.430
Although I must be innocent,

00:22:19.430 --> 00:22:23.340
nanraka no batsu wo uketeru

00:22:19.430 --> 00:22:23.340
now I am punished.

00:22:23.770 --> 00:22:29.640
jibun de maita tane de mo nai no ni

00:22:23.770 --> 00:22:29.640
I wasn't the one who sowed those seeds, but nevertheless

00:22:30.360 --> 00:22:36.550
sakimidareta hana tsumasareru

00:22:30.360 --> 00:22:36.550
I have to pull up the flowers that bloomed from them.

00:22:43.100 --> 00:22:47.740
shiranai koto to mo ienai ga

00:22:43.100 --> 00:22:47.740
I can't say I didn't know about it,

00:22:47.740 --> 00:22:52.190
katabou katsuida oboe wa nai

00:22:47.740 --> 00:22:52.190
but I don't remember taking any part in it.

00:22:52.190 --> 00:22:58.380
jiyuu wo takaku kawasareta ki mo suru ga

00:22:52.190 --> 00:22:58.380
I think my freedom cost me dearly,

00:22:58.910 --> 00:23:05.620
kokoro made yasuku utta oboe wa nai

00:22:58.910 --> 00:23:05.620
but I don't remember selling my soul so cheaply.

00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:13.670
Hey Hey kutabatte osaraba suru made

00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:13.670
Hey hey, until I die and say farewell...

00:23:14.690 --> 00:23:23.580
Hey Hey dare no te ni mo kakaranai

00:23:14.690 --> 00:23:23.580
Hey hey... no one can touch me.

00:23:25.100 --> 00:23:29.190
tooi yoru wo urotsuiteiru

00:23:25.100 --> 00:23:29.190
You probably don't know

00:23:29.190 --> 00:23:36.900
shiranai darou eien no narazu monotachi wo

00:23:29.190 --> 00:23:36.900
the eternal outlaws prowling in the distant night.
